      "writtenOn": "2020-08-24T11:17:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, but don\u0027t you risk keeping flags for 1 reboot too many?\n\nScenario intended:\n\n1. Set flags \u003d X \u003d\u003e z-state\n2. Power on 1: Read flag \u003d X; Set flags \u003d X | EC_RESET_FLAG_INITIAL_PWR\n3. Power on 2: Read flag \u003d X | EC_RESET_FLAG_INITIAL_PWR; Set flags \u003d 0\n4. Next boot: Read flag \u003d 0\n\nScenario that appears to be broken:\n\n1. Set flags \u003d X \u003d\u003e z-state\n2. Power on 1: No time to read/set flags.\n3. Power on 2: Read flag \u003d X; Set flags \u003d X | EC_RESET_FLAG_INITIAL_PWR\n4. Next boot: Read flag \u003d X | EC_RESET_FLAG_INITIAL_PWR\n\nIs there anything we can do to protect against that second scenario?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 93,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "811553f016f26f68b582458cad5e28af07040f65",
